        "procedure": "Butylsalicylate (1.05 g, 5.40 mmol) was dissolved in methanol, triethylamine (1.22 ml, 8.80 mmol) was added, and the solution was stirred at 40 °C. Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (1.372 g, 3.04 mmol) in methanol was added dropwise and the mixture was stirred for 30 min. After cooling to room temperature, a white powder of the Gd9 cluster was obtained 15 min later. Colorless single crystals for X-ray analysis were obtained from methanol.",
